OL,3,GNEWSAFirst minister 'gobsmacked' by
OL,4,ABurnham's devolution calls rejection
OL,5,
OL,6,FWales' First Minister Rhun ap Iorwerth
OL,7,Fhas declared he is "gobsmacked" after
OL,8,Fcalls for powers to be handed from
OL,9,FWestminster to Cardiff were snubbed.
OL,11,FIn a letter to ap Iorwerth, Prime
OL,12,FMinister Andy Burnham said he was "not
OL,13,Fpersuaded" by the case to devolve
OL,14,Fresponsibilities over policing and
OL,15,Fjustice, the Crown Estate and rail
OL,16,Finfrastructure to Wales.
OL,18,FThe first minister told BBC Radio Wales
OL,19,Fbreakfast that "this is about
OL,20,FWestminster saying, we decide, it
OL,21,Fdoesn't matter what the people of Wales
OL,22,Fthink".
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,435,430,260,140,0,100
